<<<
toffee. The successive forms seem tô have been taffy, toffy, toffee; it mmay be guessed that the last is due to the influence of coffee, but it is now established. together. All t. must be carefully distinguished from ALTOGETHER, often written instead of it. toilet, -ette. The word should be

completely anglicized in spelling &

sound (not -e’tte, nor twahlé’t). The —

verb, =to wash, dress, &c., is chiefly

U.S. ; adj. & p.p. -eted, see -T-, -TT-.
===
**toffee.** The successive forms seem to have been *taffy*, *toffy*, *toffee*; it may be guessed that the last is due to the influence of *coffee*, but it is now established.

**together.** *All t.* must be carefully distinguished from ^^ALTOGETHER^^, often written instead of it.

**toilet, -ette.** The word should be completely anglicized in spelling & sound (not *-e'tte*, nor *twahlĕ't*). The verb, = to wash, dress, &c., is chiefly U.S.; adj. & p.p. *-eted*, see ^^-T-, -TT-^^.
>>>

