<<<
in the following two quotations the addition of with &c. & in &c. to the participles turns the scale, & too much should have been written instead of too:—Belfast is too occupied with its own affairs, too confident of itself, to be readily stirred to any movement which would endanger its prosperity. /But he was too engrossed in Northern Europe to realize his failure. 6 TOO 2. Illogical uses. These are very
